insert into public.challenge_answers (challenge_id, correct_index, explanation, attack_technique)
select id, 1, $c$Urgent wording is a red flag, but it is not proof. The technical evidence is what matters: the sending IP is not authorized for the domain (SPF fail), the message is unsigned (no DKIM), DMARC fails, and replies would go to a free mail account instead of Microsoft. The lookalike domain hosting a login page completes the picture of a credential phishing attempt. Next steps: block the sender domain and URL, search for other recipients, and confirm nobody entered credentials.$c$, $c$T1566.002$c$ from ch
