select id, 0, $c$This is a classic download cradle. DownloadString fetches a script as text and IEX (Invoke-Expression) executes it in memory without writing a file to disk. The flags -nop (no profile), -w hidden (hidden window), and -enc (Base64 encoded command) are common evasion choices. A Word document spawning PowerShell almost always points to a malicious macro. Isolate the host, block the IP, and collect the original document.$c$, $c$T1059.001$c$ from ch
