select id, 3, $c$Plenty of legitimate software uses scheduled tasks, so the details matter. Here the task hides under a Microsoft path with a Chrome name, yet it launches svch0st.exe (zero instead of the letter o) from AppData\Roaming, a user-writable location real system binaries never run from. Running at every logon and repeating every 30 minutes is a persistence pattern, which explains why the host became active again after cleanup.$c$, $c$T1053.005$c$ from ch
